{
  "title": "Summary early-expiratory volume ratio did not establish added wheeze prediction across separate NHANES samples",
  "abstract": "Adding summary FEV0.5/FEV1 to a source-trained model containing standard volumes and midflow did not establish reliable target wheeze prediction gain: Brier difference -0.00009733, paired PSU95% interval [-0.00023149,0.00003852], NHANES2007-08 n3670 to independently sampled2011-12 n3650. This is a negative incremental-prediction test, not a biological null. Effort adjustment reversed the tiny point gain; single best-value summaries can come from different maneuvers.",
